# This repository holds exactly two things: the `hachi` Rust crate and the Lean
# proofs about its Aeneas-extracted model. Everything else in this directory --
# the ArkLib clone, the extraction binaries, and every build tree -- is either
# third-party, machine-local, or derived, and is listed below. `make setup`
# obtains the parts that are not in git.
#
# `hachi/benches/` is tracked in full, the frozen `genesis/` crate included --
# it is source, not output. No timings are committed anywhere: criterion's own
# output lands under `hachi/target/criterion`, which `target/` covers, and the
# optional `JSON=` report is covered at the root. Every figure is re-derived by
# the next run, on the machine that will act on it.


# --- Not tracked, obtained or generated locally ------------------------------
#
# No checkout below is needed to build the proofs, and none is a submodule.
# `hachi/lakefile.lean` fetches both dependencies from git and Lake keeps its
# own copies under `hachi/.lake/packages/`, at the revisions pinned in
# `hachi/lake-manifest.json`. That manifest is the only thing a clone needs.

# The one that still matters, and only for `make extract`: the charon and aeneas
# binaries that regenerate `hachi/lean/Generated.lean`. One of them blows past
# GitHub's 100 MB file limit. `make setup` downloads them.
/toolchain/

# Reference clones only, read by nothing: Lake fetches ArkLib itself, and the
# `cpoly` field layer arrives as a cargo dependency (see NOTES.md).
/ArkLib/
/AeneasCompPoly/


# --- Derived output ----------------------------------------------------------

# `make` bookkeeping: stamps recording what `make setup` has already done, and
# the `lake build` log that `make build` scans for `sorry`. Deleting it costs
# nothing but a re-run of `make setup`, which re-checks rather than re-downloads.
/.make/

# Rust build tree. Also where criterion writes, under hachi/target/criterion.
target/

# Lake build tree, and the dependency sources Lake fetches into it.
.lake/

# Compiled Lean, in case any lands outside .lake/.
*.olean
*.ilean

# Charon's output, the intermediate half of the extraction pipeline: charon
# writes hachi/generated.llbc, then aeneas turns it into
# hachi/lean/Generated.lean. `make extract` regenerates both.
#
# `lean/Generated.lean` itself IS tracked, and has to be: reproducing it needs
# the ./toolchain binaries above, which are not in the repo, so a clone that
# only has Lean must still be able to build the proofs.
*.llbc

# Bench reports. `make run-bench JSON=out.json` writes one relative to wherever
# make was invoked, which is this directory. A report is a statement about one
# machine at one moment and is worthless to a reader on another, so none of them
# is ever committed. Root-scoped: `hachi/lake-manifest.json` is tracked.
/*.json

# The frozen baseline is built as a path dependency of `hachi`, so it normally
# has no lock file of its own; running cargo inside it directly leaves one.
# `hachi/Cargo.lock` IS tracked, deliberately -- benchmark numbers are only
# comparable across runs if the dependency graph criterion is built from is
# pinned along with the toolchain.
/hachi/benches/genesis/Cargo.lock
/hachi/benches/candidate/Cargo.lock


# --- Editor, tooling and OS noise --------------------------------------------

__pycache__/
*.py[co]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Tool permissions granted on one machine.
/.claude/settings.local.json
